WEBVTT

00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:13.305
Open your company's Historical Data page on Yahoo Finance. This example is Charles Schwab, SCHW

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:17.109
Select the dates to choose the days you need

00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:27.062
Type a start date a few days before the move and an end date a few days after

00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:34.416
Select Done

00:00:34.416 --> 00:00:40.445
Each row is one trading day, newest at the top. Find the last day before the move began

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:45.764
Its number in the Close column is that day's close: 76.20 on March 8

00:00:45.764 --> 00:00:51.398
Then find the close on the day the move ended: 51.91 on March 13

00:00:51.398 --> 00:00:55.407
Do the same for the S&P 500, ticker ^GSPC, on the same two days
